<title>ITALY: Italian CPI 1.6 pct yr/yr in July - Istat.</title>
<headline>Italian CPI 1.6 pct yr/yr in July - Istat.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Office (ISTAT) reported the following consumer inflation details:</p>
<p> ITALIAN INFLATION	   July 97    June 97	July 96</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index rise	 0.0	  0.0	 -0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation	     1.6	  1.4	  3.6</p>
<p> Index (Base 1996)	    105.7	105.7	104.0</p>
<p>Istat said that including tobacco costs in the inflation data gave a CPI rate of 1.6 percent for July.  </p>
<p>ISTAT gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown.</p>
<p> Sector			   Index	   mo/mo (%)    yr/yr (%)</p>
<p> Food (without tabacco)     104.0	    -0.2	   -1.0</p>
<p> Clothing			 106.8	     0.0	    2.4</p>
<p> Housing,Electricity,Fuel   109.6	     0.3	    5.9</p>
<p> Domestic goods		 105.4	     0.0	    1.4</p>
<p> Health spending		105.9	     0.0	    3.3</p>
<p> Transport			106.4	     0.1	    1.4</p>
<p> Recreation		     102.8	    -0.2	    0.5</p>
<p> Education			107.5	     0.0	    3.4</p>
<p> Hotels, restaurants	  106.6	     0.0	    2.1</p>
<p> Other goods,service	  104.9	    -0.3	    1.7</p>
<p>(including communications)</p>
